    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (68.98) and **Taylor Ward** (68.75) anchor our lineup, serving as the strongest daily plays due to their high floors and advantageous matchups. **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** benefits from a steady matchup against Suter, while **Taylor Ward** is a high-upside play against Weathers; the latter is particularly boosted by a favorable park factor (+16%) and a strong platoon edge (+9%). Furthermore, we are aggressively targeting the matchup against Roki Sasaki, whose 5.30 xERA makes him a prime target for our core hitters. Consequently, **Luis Arraez** (66.78), **Jung Hoo Lee** (65.65), and **Matt Chapman** (65.37) all receive significant bumps, as their collective ability to capitalize on Sasaki\u2019s high-velocity, high-mistake profile makes them essential starts today.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involves our rotation of utility options, as **Jeremiah Jackson** (47.70) narrowly edged out the remaining depth to claim the MI spot. While **Jeremiah Jackson** is anchored at the bottom of the order, his projection is propped up by a park-factor boost and, crucially, a minor efficiency gain for the potential to steal bases against a slow-delivering pitcher. Meanwhile, **Will Smith** (49.41) remains a concern; he is active but his score is suppressed by a difficult assignment against a 2.60 xERA arm in Trevor McDonald, placing him in the marginal category. We continue to monitor the status of **Yainer Diaz**, who remains sidelined on the IL, alongside **Lawrence Butler**, **Bryson Stott**, and **Tyler Freeman**, all of whom are unavailable due to team off-days. With **Gleyber Torres**, **Wenceel Perez**, **Masyn Winn**, and **Gavin Sheets** also currently outside the optimal construction, we are relying on the high-contact profiles of **Brendan Donovan** and **Daulton Varsho** to stabilize our AVG category while chasing the stolen base upside inherent in today\u2019s favorable SP matchups.",
